# Keep docker build contexts source-only. Every Dockerfile in this repo
# installs its own dependencies inside the builder stage (yarn), so host
# node_modules trees are pure context weight — and worse, they can carry
# symlinks that ESCAPE the context: a host `yarn link` produces
# ui/node_modules/komodo_client -> ~/.config/yarn/link/komodo_client, which
# (a) points outside the context and (b) cycles back into it via the link
# target. Podman's context sender fails the whole build on such a symlink
# ("invalid symlink"), where docker would silently skip it. Observed
# 2026-10-02 building compose/oidc-dev/core-ui.Dockerfile (context = repo
# root); context went from ~119 MB streamed to source-only.
.git
**/node_modules
